## Extremely Niche Nature of This Work

This project involves advanced algebraic structures (including rotations in **sedenions** and other hypercomplex numbers), transcendental functions evaluated in high-precision floating-point arithmetic, and deliberate exploitation of IEEE 754 rounding errors in real hardware.

**Fewer than 10–20 people on the planet** actively work on or deeply understand the combination of:
- transcendental floating-point arithmetic on exotic algebras (sedenions, octonions etc.)
- controlled non-unitary operations via rounding errors
- rotations of such objects in cryptographic/data-transformation contexts

The vast majority of mathematicians, cryptographers and programmers still operate within the paradigm of real/complex numbers and assume perfect precision – which is why nobody has built anything quite like this before.

**If you want to implement or extend this work correctly – you probably need someone who already understands these concepts.**  
This is not trivial mathematics. It is a very specialized, almost esoteric domain.

